{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview","id":1043186,"title":"Any Doubts about the Theoi having Shapeshifting as their Pantheon Purview?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-03T15:28:41-08:00","id":1043186,"title":"Any Doubts about the Theoi having Shapeshifting as their Pantheon Purview?","content":"So I think this will work out and be pretty cool, It can be more fun then the simple arete we had before. But I still have doubts. I mean a lot of peoples essentially viewed the gods as being able to take forms different from man. I think the thing is we just have more examples of Gods doing stuff in general for the Theoi because well there are a lot of Greek/Roman/Etruscan legends that survived compared to say the Aesir.<br /> <br /> I mean it seemed Zeus had a greater degree of shapeshifting in his legends, what with turning ants into men, turning people into cows, turning himself into a &quot;Golden Shower&quot;. But many of the other Gods were more toned down, they were usually just invisible or in the form of wind or air. Yeah Proteus could change form but that was his thing, representing the fluid nature of water. But it can be argued many of the other Pantheons have just as mutable shape as the Greek Myths. Like Zeus disguising himself as a mortal vagabond to observe Lykan Odin did this all the time as well, along with the rest of his pantheon. Sigurd was observed by gods in the form of birds. Loki turned into birds, and nuts, and horses, even Thor disgused himself as a boy when he went fishing.<br /> <br /> Vishnu manifested as everything from a Dwarf, to a Boar, to a fishman or a boy, arguably more mutable then Zeus' myths.<br /> <br /> So I will fully embrace their schtik as shapeshifters, I still have the nagging in the back of my head that giving them Shapeshifting as their &quot;thing&quot; seems a lot like giving Jotunblut to the Aesir. Something that was viewed as a clever new interpretation to make them stand out but really having some questionable issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:37:38-08:00","id":1043193,"title":"","content":"I think it makes perfect sense so long as their PSP also involves transforming others as well as themselves; Greek myth is not only rife with the gods taking varied shape, but transforming others (into animals, monsters, other sexes, etc) as punishment, reward, or escape. Other gods and mortals do it as well, but I'm struggling to see something else that would fit the Theoi better.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:40:17-08:00","id":1043198,"title":"","content":"Well you know... arete... just reimagine it as something different from Legendary Attribute lite...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:16:34-08:00","id":1043224,"title":"","content":"I followed the mental reasoning given when the Theoi were previewed. And while yeah, the Aesir had Loki as a shapeshifter... But honestly? If you look at the overall collection of the Greek and Roman myths, then you'll see that a LOT of them involve someone changing themselves, someone transforming someone else, or <i>both</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;You like your own appearance? You're a flower now!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't escape me, I'm a shower of golden coins!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're a monster now!&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, it happens in pretty much all myth... But in the Greek legends I'm familiar with it happens <i>a LOT</i>. I can see why they chose it. Though I'm curious what the innate power and some of the Boons are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:23:28-08:00","id":1043229,"title":"","content":"Well to me that just seemed more like we have more surviving Greek stories.<br /> <br /> I mean we still have this in the very few surviving Norse Myths. Not just Loki turning himself into a bird and another into an acorn. We have Odin turning into a snake to get mead. We have Odin and his brothers grabbing primordial maggots and they become dwarves, turning one of his Nephews into a Wolf, turning brains into clouds, lots of wonky stuff.<br /> <br /> But yeah I do see what you mean and that is why I am okay with shapeshifting being their thing, but it does seem a smidgeon contrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:33:47-08:00","id":1043238,"title":"","content":"<i>Metamorphoses</i> is a classic for a reason. What else would you suggest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:46:27-08:00","id":1043244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043198#post1043198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you know... arete... just reimagine it as something different from Legendary Attribute lite...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean when does Hephaestus or Heracles shapeshift themselves or others, besides the ambiguity of their size.<br /> <br /> But it works. In a lot of ways people view the Greek gods as the most Defaulty/Vanilla/Generic of the gods because Familiarity kind of does that. So give it a try, if they think it is more fun then Arete by all means. I mean I don't even really know how the rules and powers will look till I read the whole book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:49:15-08:00","id":1043245,"title":"","content":"Woohoo, shapeshifting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Really, the whole Arete thing from 1st edition was just excessive baggage to a system that was already broken with OP ridiculousness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although this now brings up another concern as to what the Chinese PSP is going to be. Unless I'm mistaken, their PSP in 1st edition was all about transformation. One of their god level powers even gives you the option to pretty much remake any character from the ground up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-03-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:53:51-08:00","id":1043247,"title":"","content":"Yeah lot of lazy decisions that didn't pan out well in first ed. :P<br /> <br /> But one of things I'm worried about for instance, is if we give the Theoi shapeshifting will the setting subtlely try to hobble all the other Pantheons' shapeshifting options to emphasize the Theoi's unique niche? I mean tossing a stone over your shoulder to recreate humanity after the flood was something they did, but will that mean you will not really be doing that with other pantheons? Will Loki be worse at shapeshifting then a random Theoi like Apollo or will he be able to compete with Zeus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:02:24-08:00","id":1043253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043247#post1043247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah lot of lazy decisions that didn't pan out well in first ed. :P<br /> <br /> But one of things I'm worried about for instance, is if we give the Theoi shapeshifting will the setting subtlely try to hobble all the other Pantheons' shapeshifting options to emphasize the Theoi's unique niche? I mean tossing a stone over your shoulder to recreate humanity after the flood was something they did, but will that mean you will not really be doing that with other pantheons? Will Loki be worse at shapeshifting then a random Theoi like Apollo or will he be able to compete with Zeus?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think (hope) that there will be ways in which the other pantheons can achieve shapeshifting if they so wish. But the Theoi will be the masters of it. And that kind of makes sense, because a lot of classical legends from their culture depict creatures with physiology from multiple different species blended together, which sounds like it could be the work of somebody who's highly talented with altering the physical form.<br /> <br /> And I do suspect that some of their abilities will involve transforming other people. The Theoi were quite fond of turning people into trees, supposedly as a means of protecting them from rapists... Unfortunately, I don't know of any stories in which they reverse the transformation, basically leaving the innocent victim rooted to the ground as a plant for the rest of their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:42:42-08:00","id":1043272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043245#post1043245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woohoo, shapeshifting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />Although this now brings up another concern as to what the Chinese PSP is going to be. Unless I'm mistaken, their PSP in 1st edition was all about transformation. One of their god level powers even gives you the option to pretty much remake any character from the ground up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the PSP was partially teased in a preview. Looks like the Shen's PSP powers are all about bureaucracy. Seriously, the passive benefit is amazing for day-to-day affairs. Scions of the Shen are never bogged down with mortal bureaucracy. Like, their passports get approved at the fastest speeds, and they never have to wait too long at the DMV.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:53:05-08:00","id":1043277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043247#post1043247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah lot of lazy decisions that didn't pan out well in first ed. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do not demean the efforts of the creators of Scion first edition. There are other ways to express your opinions. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:57:59-08:00","id":1043279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043272#post1043272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the PSP was partially teased in a preview. Looks like the Shen's PSP powers are all about bureaucracy. Seriously, the passive benefit is amazing for day-to-day affairs. Scions of the Shen are never bogged down with mortal bureaucracy. Like, their passports get approved at the fastest speeds, and they never have to wait too long at the DMV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Gods damn it!<br /> <br /> Well, that's one way to recruit defectors to your side of the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:10:58-08:00","id":1043286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043247#post1043247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah lot of lazy decisions that didn't pan out well in first ed. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer to think of it as &quot;Scion 1e had some good ideas that got weighed down at higher tiers... And unlike Exalted didn't have the benefit of such intense errata&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:11:27-08:00","id":1043358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview#post1043186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think this will work out and be pretty cool, It can be more fun then the simple arete we had before. But I still have doubts. I mean a lot of peoples essentially viewed the gods as being able to take forms different from man. I think the thing is we just have more examples of Gods doing stuff in general for the Theoi because well there are a lot of Greek/Roman/Etruscan legends that survived compared to say the Aesir.<br /> <br /> I mean it seemed Zeus had a greater degree of shapeshifting in his legends, what with turning ants into men, turning people into cows, turning himself into a &quot;Golden Shower&quot;. But many of the other Gods were more toned down, they were usually just invisible or in the form of wind or air. Yeah Proteus could change form but that was his thing, representing the fluid nature of water. But it can be argued many of the other Pantheons have just as mutable shape as the Greek Myths. Like Zeus disguising himself as a mortal vagabond to observe Lykan Odin did this all the time as well, along with the rest of his pantheon. Sigurd was observed by gods in the form of birds. Loki turned into birds, and nuts, and horses, even Thor disgused himself as a boy when he went fishing.<br /> <br /> Vishnu manifested as everything from a Dwarf, to a Boar, to a fishman or a boy, arguably more mutable then Zeus' myths.<br /> <br /> So I will fully embrace their schtik as shapeshifters, I still have the nagging in the back of my head that giving them Shapeshifting as their &quot;thing&quot; seems a lot like giving Jotunblut to the Aesir. Something that was viewed as a clever new interpretation to make them stand out but really having some questionable issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Regarding Vishnu...the Hindu Gods rarely if ever shape-shift...what you're describing is Incarnation, Avataran, not Shape-shifting, which is a thing Asura tend to do more often than not. Vishnu's not <i>turning INTO</i> a boar, he's manifesting an Incarnation of himself that <b>IS</b> a boar. It's a fundamental difference of PSP Philosophy. Metamorphosis is about changing how things are, Yoga is about union with the Supreme Reality of Brahman...having united with the underlying Reality of all things, Vishnu already <i>IS</i> all things, and he is therefore just spawning off a part of him that is a boar. Similarly when Parvati turns into Kali, or vice versa, she's not shape-shifting to just look different...Parvati and Kali are two aspects of the same Goddess, the gentle nurturing Mother and Nature Red in tooth and Claw all in One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T22:01:12-08:00","id":1043387,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Hanuman is a shapeshifter, Raskshasa are shapeshifters - the Avatars of Vishnu not so much. At most you have cases like Krishna who can have a mortal appearance and a revealed true divine appearance. Avatars aren't shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T22:08:29-08:00","id":1043389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043198#post1043198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you know... arete... just reimagine it as something different from Legendary Attribute lite...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The fact of the matter is that while Greek Mythic figures are often superhumanly skilled - that's no more the case than with culture heroes in any other mythic tradition. Shapeshifting themselves and others freely is a much more distinct theme in Greek Myth. You do find figures like Loki and Hanuman in other cultures, but they're usually unique in that role, while for the Olympians it's an inherent facet of godhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:16:03-08:00","id":1043481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043389#post1043389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is that while Greek Mythic figures are often superhumanly skilled - that's no more the case than with culture heroes in any other mythic tradition. Shapeshifting themselves and others freely is a much more distinct theme in Greek Myth. You do find figures like Loki and Hanuman in other cultures, but they're usually unique in that role, while for the Olympians it's an inherent facet of godhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not unique to Loki though in the Aesir, it seems to be part of Godhood and divine knowledge of Runes, Rig, Odin, Freyja, Frigg, gods they could shapeshift. Polynesian cultural heroes could also shapeshift much more notably, the Kapua.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And its debateable Avataras don't count as shapeshifting, one could argue things like Kapua aren't shapeshifting then either because they have double bodies. And Avataras are arguably different then Incarnations, which are flesh and imperfect, while Avataras are mythical and perfect.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I'm not arguing other Pantheons should have Shapeshifting just that its not a given that it seperates Theoi from other gods. I mean the Alchemies Sun Wu Kong Learned specifically seem to involve this, and it is not supposed to be at all limited to him, he just mastered it. Gods often can take the form of Animals or Winds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:41:48-08:00","id":1043495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043277#post1043277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please do not demean the efforts of the creators of Scion first edition. There are other ways to express your opinions. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, I retract my sentiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:50:16-08:00","id":1043498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043481#post1043481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And its debateable Avataras don't count as shapeshifting, one could argue things like Kapua aren't shapeshifting then either because they have double bodies. And Avataras are arguably different then Incarnations, which are flesh and imperfect, while Avataras are mythical and perfect.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reality is an illusion, all things are one with each other. I wouldn't call that shapeshifting, rather it seems more like manifestation.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Do not try to bend the spoon, that's impossible. Instead, only try to realize the truth.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What truth?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;There is no spoon...&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;There is no spoon?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Then you'll see that it is not the spoon that bends, it is only yourself.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-04-2017, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:16:15-08:00","id":1043505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043481#post1043481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And its debateable Avataras don't count as shapeshifting, one could argue things like Kapua aren't shapeshifting then either because they have double bodies. And Avataras are arguably different then Incarnations, which are flesh and imperfect, while Avataras are mythical and perfect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about Polynesian mythology to make any comment on Kapua, but Avatara aren't Shape-shifting...especially not in Vishnu's case where the Avatara has a separate existence and does things apart from Vishnu himself whilst of course still being him. There's a story in southern India where Vishnu goes to Varaha for marriage advice whilst he and Lakshmi are going through a rough patch i.e. she sent him into a coma for long enough for termites to build mounds over him and he woke up to an axe to the face. I'm not sure if this marital dispute is more or less horrifying than the time Sarasvati sent a giant snake to murder her husband or the time Parvati just straight up <b>ate</b> hers, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't know nearly enough about the Incarnations system yet to make any comment on how well it fits the needs of the Hindu Gods Avataran...if it is different, then creating Avatara is probably just a PSP Boon for them, attained through Yoga. My personal theory is the the Parvati Kali type thing is a God Level Yoga Boon that allows multiple Mantles of teh same Hindu God to manifest as Separate Beings, while still being the same being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 02-04-2017, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:10:45-08:00","id":1043525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043505#post1043505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know enough about Polynesian mythology to make any comment on Kapua, but Avatara aren't Shape-shifting...especially not in Vishnu's case where the Avatara has a separate existence and does things apart from Vishnu himself whilst of course still being him. There's a story in southern India where Vishnu goes to Varaha for marriage advice whilst he and Lakshmi are going through a rough patch i.e. she sent him into a coma for long enough for termites to build mounds over him and he woke up to an axe to the face. I'm not sure if this marital dispute is more or less horrifying than the time Sarasvati sent a giant snake to murder her husband or the time Parvati just straight up <b>ate</b> hers, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't know nearly enough about the Incarnations system yet to make any comment on how well it fits the needs of the Hindu Gods Avataran...if it is different, then creating Avatara is probably just a PSP Boon for them, attained through Yoga. My personal theory is the the Parvati Kali type thing is a God Level Yoga Boon that allows multiple Mantles of teh same Hindu God to manifest as Separate Beings, while still being the same being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I don't understand how the first paragraph is particularly relevant.<br /> <br /> But I am not talking about the gamelines incarnation/avatar system, I am talking about the theological comparisons were Christians for instance refer to Jesus as an incarnation of God, so they believe translations into english wouldn't use Incarnation in place of Avataras because they are beings of imperfect flesh while Avataras are mythical aspects.<br /> <br /> But ultimately would you use one of the power systems to represent being able to take the form of an Animal, like a god have the Beast Purview, or some sort of Pantheon specific Purview? If so then these arguments are semantics about the term shapeshifting, because then all you have to do is just call it having multiple shapes and boom argument goes back on track.<br /> <br /> But the Ovid is a good citation for giving the Theoi this power as their schtick, as it is rife with changing of shapes of ones self and others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:28:27-08:00","id":1043533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043525#post1043525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I don't understand how the first paragraph is particularly relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first paragraph was me giving some more reasons why I thought Avatara isn't Shapeshifting before veering off into unrelated territory and veering back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043525#post1043525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I am not talking about the gamelines incarnation/avatar system, I am talking about the theological comparisons were Christians for instance refer to Jesus as an incarnation of God, so they believe translations into english wouldn't use Incarnation in place of Avataras because they are beings of imperfect flesh while Avataras are mythical aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I didn't understand the context of original your quote and I apologize. I'm not particularly familiar with Christian Theology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043525#post1043525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But ultimately would you use one of the power systems to represent being able to take the form of an Animal, like a god have the Beast Purview, or some sort of Pantheon specific Purview? If so then these arguments are semantics about the term shapeshifting, because then all you have to do is just call it having multiple shapes and boom argument goes back on track.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt 'turning in to an animal' would be a Metamorphosis boon...look at the Aztec PSP boons...they're not about <i>making</i> sacrifices, they're about gaining additional benefits <i>from</i> the base sacrifice system already in place. Similarly I would expect that actual Metamorphosis Boons don't do shape-shifting, they refine it. Actual shape-shifting Powers should probably be in the Trickster Knack Tree and Animal or Deception Purviews, since it's Trickster Gods and Animal Gods and Illusion Gods who moistly do shapeshifting in myth, as opposed to the Theoi where everyone irrespective of Calling changes shape. Hell, perhaps the Innate Power of Metamorphosis is that it lets Scions access the Shapeshifting powers irrespective of Calling?<br /> <br /> Having written that I'm honestly beginning to think it it's best to wait to see the Metamorphosis Purview before deciding on how generic or unique it makes the Greeks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043525#post1043525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Ovid is a good citation for giving the Theoi this power as their schtick, as it is rife with changing of shapes of ones self and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I agree with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:38:36-08:00","id":1043541,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Metamorphosis will allow you to shapeshift without other powers, that way you don't need to give Athena other powers to turn Arachne into a spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:37:55-08:00","id":1043608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043525#post1043525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But I am not talking about the gamelines incarnation/avatar system, I am talking about the theological comparisons were Christians for instance refer to Jesus as an incarnation of God, so they believe translations into english wouldn't use Incarnation in place of Avataras because they are beings of imperfect flesh while Avataras are mythical aspects.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually depends on what sect or denomination of Christianity you're talking about (and there are, like 20,000 of them). Some of them (such as the Catholics) believe that Jesus and YHVH are the same person. Others believe that Jesus is YHVH's son and therefor, they'd be two different entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043541#post1043541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Metamorphosis will allow you to shapeshift without other powers, that way you don't need to give Athena other powers to turn Arachne into a spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally holding out hope that 2nd Edition Theoi get a power similar to Ixion's, in which they're able to create monsters. Hell, their mythology is chalk full of them having done just that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-04-2017, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:14:53-08:00","id":1043625,"title":"","content":"Theoi Signature Purview: Metamorphosis<br /> The mythos of the Theoi is replete with tales of transformation, old forms changed into new entities. Gods take on the shapes of animals and humans, weather and geography, even abstract forms such as thoughts or emotions. They also transform others, turning foes into beasts, lovers into flowers, and heroes into constellations. This Purview governs both kinds of transformations, allowing Theoi Scions to emulate their parents\u2019 mutability. <br /> Innate Power: Your mutable nature lends itself to disguise. When you conceal your identity by any means, trivial characters automatically fail to see through your deception. When you roll to disguise yourself or present yourself as someone else, you ignore any Complications from changing height, size, race, sex, or even species.<br /> Change Shape<br /> Cost: Spend 1 Legend<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Subject: Self<br /> Action: Simple<br /> You take on a form that is symbolically associated with one of your other Purviews. For example, Zeus drew on the associations of the Sky Purview to become all sorts of birds, a shower of gold, and a bull (which sounds a great deal like thunder, up close). This transformation is perfect in the details and undetectable through non-magical means, but doesn\u2019t alter any of your Attributes, Skills, or other traits. However, depending on the form you assume, you can gain the following benefits:<br /> One of: +1 Size, +1 Pace, or +1 Durability. <br /> Any special forms of movement that shape possesses.<br /> Any natural attacks that shape possesses.<br /> Any miscellaneous abilities the Storyguide decides the shape should have, like a cloud being able to rain.<br /> I Stab The Cloud<br /> Theoi Scions can\u2019t become invulnerable by taking on forms that are normally invalid targets for attacks\u2014they still use their Defense and Stress boxes like normal. The resulting Injury Complications (p. XX) can be more abstract to suit the form\u2014a cloud might be \u201cDissipated\u201d\u2014but revert to more mundane injuries upon returning to human form. If you want to emphasize the difficulty of attacking what you\u2019ve turned into, represent that with increased Durability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:18:17-08:00","id":1043626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally holding out hope that 2nd Edition Theoi get a power similar to Ixion's, in which they're able to create monsters. Hell, their mythology is chalk full of them having done just that!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Demigod-level Boon of their Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:46:19-08:00","id":1043634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043626#post1043626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a Demigod-level Boon of their Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NICE! Gonna have fun screwing with people who anger my characters! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T15:34:47-08:00","id":1043752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043625#post1043625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Innate Power: Your mutable nature lends itself to disguise. When you conceal your identity by any means, trivial characters automatically fail to see through your deception. When you roll to disguise yourself or present yourself as someone else, you ignore any Complications from changing height, size, race, sex, or even species.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait... I can just put on a pair of glasses and say I'm a mild-mannered reporter, and nobody knows the difference?<br /> <br /> *Cue John Williams.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T16:29:32-08:00","id":1043764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043752#post1043752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait... I can just put on a pair of glasses and say I'm a mild-mannered reporter, and nobody knows the difference?<br /> <br /> *Cue John Williams.*</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also pretend to be a totally innocent animal who doesn't know nothin' about any 'sleeping with the judge's daughter' with a bit of fake whiskers drawn on the face and cat ear headwear.<br /> <br /> Keeping that skeevy Theoi tradition alive in the modern day even without turning into other things directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T16:37:04-08:00","id":1043767,"title":"","content":"Okay, I demand that Metamorphosis have a power called &quot;This Isn't Even My Final Form!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T16:55:44-08:00","id":1043771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043767#post1043767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I demand that Metamorphosis have a power called &quot;This Isn't Even My Final Form!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I demand it has a power called &quot;They Went That-A-Way!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T07:21:26-08:00","id":1043974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good thinking making sure it says *other* Purviews, because if it just said &quot;symbolically associated with one of your Purviews&quot;, I know there would be players trying to be clever by insisting that every imaginable form is symbolically associated with the Transformation Purview itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be shenanigans! And one of your other purviews being the point of the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T07:54:01-08:00","id":1043983,"title":"","content":"Metamorphosis + Earth = An animated statue made of flawless marble<br /> <br /> <br /> Metamorphosis + Water = A reflection in a clear pool<br /> <br /> <br /> Metamorphosis + Sky = A surprisingly accurate formation of clouds<br /> <br /> <br /> Metamorphosis + Fire = A silhouette dancing in the flames of a warm hearth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:26:45-08:00","id":1044021,"title":"","content":"That's not exactly what I was expecting, but I really like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was a little worried that PSPs like Metamorphosis and Possession might feel a little too 'one-track' as compared to some of the others, but given this Purview evolves into monster-spawning, looks like I had no reason to be worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:00:42-08:00","id":1044044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1044021#post1044021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not exactly what I was expecting, but I really like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was a little worried that PSPs like Metamorphosis and Possession might feel a little too 'one-track' as compared to some of the others, but given this Purview evolves into monster-spawning, looks like I had no reason to be worried.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Monster spawning alone makes it worth adding to the repertoire!<br /> <br /> Also, worth noting the things I listed above were just examples that I personally came up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T04:15:13-08:00","id":1045679,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Tricksters with large form libraries (like Sun Wukong and Loki) will have a specific Shapeshifting purview (that isn't Metamorphoses of course)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T04:39:19-08:00","id":1045685,"title":"","content":"They have specific Immortal Trickster Knacks that allow them to augment disguises and make them real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T04:58:55-08:00","id":1045687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1045679#post1045679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Tricksters with large form libraries (like Sun Wukong and Loki) will have a specific Shapeshifting purview (that isn't Metamorphoses of course)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They should. Part of Sun Wukong's entire legend is that he has 72 transformations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T05:32:22-08:00","id":1045698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1045685#post1045685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have specific Immortal Trickster Knacks that allow them to augment disguises and make them real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that sounds neat. Looking forward to reading about that then. (I suppose the Tricksters with more Iconic shapes like Anansi or Coyote will have their Shapeshifting provided for by their Animal specific Purview)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:50:35-08:00","id":1046486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1043245#post1043245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woohoo, shapeshifting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Really, the whole Arete thing from 1st edition was just excessive baggage to a system that was already broken with OP ridiculousness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although this now brings up another concern as to what the Chinese PSP is going to be. Unless I'm mistaken, their PSP in 1st edition was all about transformation. One of their god level powers even gives you the option to pretty much remake any character from the ground up!</div> </div> </div> </div>When I wrote my own capsule explanations of pantheons, their Virtues and their PSPs for my players, here's how I explained the basis of Srete:<br /> ------<br /> Arete<br /> How did little city-states in Greece and Italy rise to conquer half the ancient World and shape all civilization to come? Their people did it by being the best: the best generals, such as Alexander and Julius Caesar; the best savants, such as Aristotle and Archimedes; the best politicians, such as Pericles and Augustus; the best authors to propagate their tales and deeds, such as Homer and Virgil; the best at <i>being the best</i>. The Dodekatheon\u2019s special Purview takes its name from the Greek word for excellence, Arete. Gods easily surpass mortal skill, but Dodekatheon members surpass even other Gods \u2014 at least in a few chosen fields. Dodekatheon characters buy Arete to increase their prowess at selected endeavors even higher than what they achieve through Abilities, Attributes and Epic Attributes. Many Dodekatheon are considerably more powerful than their lists of associated Epic Attributes and Purviews would suggest, because of their Arete with numerous mundane Abilities.<br /> ------<br /> So I don't think it was a bad conceptual choice (especially after I rewrote Arete to make it less of a point sink). But as I found out running my campaign, the dice engine shows strain even at Legend 4, and adding another source of bonus successes just does not help. So I think that Arete could only &quot;work&quot; as the PSP for the Greco-Roman Gods with a radical reworking of underlying systems. (Which I gather has been done, though I haven't followed the teasers.)<br /> <br /> Metamorphosis is such a common theme through Classical mythology that a Purview for it is at least as strong a concept, though, if not stronger. But as Nyrufa and others have pointed out, transformation and self-transformation are important in other mythologies, too -- including Chinese mythology.<br /> <br /> Taiyi, the PSP I created for the Shen back in Scion Companion, does indeed involve a great deal of transformation and self-transformation. (It does other things, too.) I designed it to emulate the feats I found Gods and immortals doing in my research of Chinese mythology -- many Boons or examples of their use are taken directly from Chinese sources, especially the Fengshen Yanyi -- and I did my best to tie it all together through Taoist metaphysics, which is all about the mutability of forms and energies.<br /> <br /> A replacement PSP based on bureaucracy? Well, I'll have to see the final result before I venture an opinion. At that time, I'll examine it based on my own research in Chinese mythology. And I may be back here, asking for a list of sources and the reasons for design choices.<br /> <br /> At this point, though, I wonder if the whole premise of the Pantheon-Specific Purview is a good one. Like, Japanese mythology is not the only one to feature a multifarious, pantheistic spirit world, so shouldn't a Purview based on interacting with such spirits be general? Transformation and self-transformation, likewise. Or are PSPs no longer quite so specific?<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T15:30:03-08:00","id":1046503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1046486#post1046486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I wrote my own capsule explanations of pantheons, their Virtues and their PSPs for my players, here's how I explained the basis of Srete:<br /> ------<br /> Arete<br /> How did little city-states in Greece and Italy rise to conquer half the ancient World and shape all civilization to come? Their people did it by being the best: the best generals, such as Alexander and Julius Caesar; the best savants, such as Aristotle and Archimedes; the best politicians, such as Pericles and Augustus; the best authors to propagate their tales and deeds, such as Homer and Virgil; the best at <i>being the best</i>. The Dodekatheon\u2019s special Purview takes its name from the Greek word for excellence, Arete. Gods easily surpass mortal skill, but Dodekatheon members surpass even other Gods \u2014 at least in a few chosen fields. Dodekatheon characters buy Arete to increase their prowess at selected endeavors even higher than what they achieve through Abilities, Attributes and Epic Attributes. Many Dodekatheon are considerably more powerful than their lists of associated Epic Attributes and Purviews would suggest, because of their Arete with numerous mundane Abilities.<br /> ------<br /> So I don't think it was a bad conceptual choice (especially after I rewrote Arete to make it less of a point sink). But as I found out running my campaign, the dice engine shows strain even at Legend 4, and adding another source of bonus successes just does not help. So I think that Arete could only &quot;work&quot; as the PSP for the Greco-Roman Gods with a radical reworking of underlying systems. (Which I gather has been done, though I haven't followed the teasers.)<br /> <br /> Metamorphosis is such a common theme through Classical mythology that a Purview for it is at least as strong a concept, though, if not stronger. But as Nyrufa and others have pointed out, transformation and self-transformation are important in other mythologies, too -- including Chinese mythology.<br /> <br /> Taiyi, the PSP I created for the Shen back in Scion Companion, does indeed involve a great deal of transformation and self-transformation. (It does other things, too.) I designed it to emulate the feats I found Gods and immortals doing in my research of Chinese mythology -- many Boons or examples of their use are taken directly from Chinese sources, especially the Fengshen Yanyi -- and I did my best to tie it all together through Taoist metaphysics, which is all about the mutability of forms and energies.<br /> <br /> A replacement PSP based on bureaucracy? Well, I'll have to see the final result before I venture an opinion. At that time, I'll examine it based on my own research in Chinese mythology. And I may be back here, asking for a list of sources and the reasons for design choices.<br /> <br /> At this point, though, I wonder if the whole premise of the Pantheon-Specific Purview is a good one. Like, Japanese mythology is not the only one to feature a multifarious, pantheistic spirit world, so shouldn't a Purview based on interacting with such spirits be general? Transformation and self-transformation, likewise. Or are PSPs no longer quite so specific?<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm happy there's an entire purview dedicated to the art of shapeshifting, but like you, I don't keep up to date on the teasers, so I'm skeptical on it being a PSp exclusive to the Greeks. Mythology is loaded to the brim with gods, goddesses, heroes, villains, demons, and everything else having the power to change its shape. So unless they come up with a very convincing explanation for why the Theoi, of all pantheons, gets special dibs on it, I'm a bit hesitant to approve of its PSP element.<br /> <br /> I mean you can mimic the effects of shapeshifting with the Animal, Health and Illusion (If it's still in use) Purviews, I guess. But then why have shapeshifting if three other Purviews can accomplish the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T16:39:40-08:00","id":1046522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043186-any-doubts-about-the-theoi-having-shapeshifting-as-their-pantheon-purview?p=1046486#post1046486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, though, I wonder if the whole premise of the Pantheon-Specific Purview is a good one. Like, Japanese mythology is not the only one to feature a multifarious, pantheistic spirit world, so shouldn't a Purview based on interacting with such spirits be general? Transformation and self-transformation, likewise. Or are PSPs no longer quite so specific?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to derail the thread, but that's actually a really good question that I don't... know if is asked often enough. I personally think PsPs totally belong, but there has never really been any unifying idea of what a PsP is, and a lot of the time the PsP isn't really actually unique to the Pantheon such as the old Kami or Loa PsPs, both concepts being pretty common globally. I think PsPs flourish when they are able to 'latch onto' a specific <i>cultural</i> detail of that Pantheon and sort of bring it to life. So, the Tuatha having an obsessive set of powers based on their social standing, the Teotl needing blood to fuel themselves, the Shiunesh needing mortals to wait on them hand and foot. A PsP that alters an existing mechanical system, like giving the Orisha and the Aesir slightly different versions of the base Fate system for example, I think is the sort of are a PsP can really... exist well? It's sort of hard to explain. I don't know if big flashy powers work, but sort of a more cosmological approach, letting each Pantheon's 'really unique cultural detail' flourish mechanically.<br /> <br /> PsPs that are more than just a set of powers I feel have always been the best. It can take some real work to make it mechanically good, but the opportunities well crafted PsPs can provide are awesome. I like the idea of the Shen PsP being based around the internal Pantheon bureaucratic system, at least how I imagine it, especially at higher levels. The Shen are tricky, we've talked about them before, spanning millennium, and several distinct religious and philosophical positions. Tapping into the bureaucracy of the cosmology I think could be really amazing to differentiate the Shen, while... like, sort of side stepping the mess that their whole system is otherwise? I'm imagining things like Demigod Boons giving you a weird minor position in the Celestial Bureaucracy which has some associated responsibilities for the Scion, but also giving them a system to tap into.<br /> <br /> Although, I <i>will</i> admit I'm honestly just a huge sucker for fancy titles which I'm hoping are lurking somewhere in the God-level of that PsP. The Arch-Bursar of Unknown Queries or other appropriately True-Fey-y titles, just love that stuff, no clue why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-09-2017, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}